  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nUpper level ridge axis will be pushed east into the Great\nPlains due to a trough moving onshore in southern Canada on\nThursday. This trough moving northeastward has already increased\nthe wind aloft, but will do even more on Thursday, with the\nstronger wind reaching the surface. The strong wind lets up\nslightly Fri, but then returns Sat. \n\nTemperatures are still inching upward through Thu afternoon, but\nthe trough and its associated surface cold front will bring\ntemperatures down for Fri and more on Sat. \n\nIsolated thunderstorms continue to be a problem with southwest\nairflow, but the more westerly airflow behind the trough on Sat\nand Sun will start a drying out with western portions of the\nforecast area out of the thunderstorm threat on some of those\ndays.\n\nTemperatures go back to little change after Sat.",
